00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.768
- Happiness is a byproduct,

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.340
not an actual destination.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.744
And so people have this
misconception that they're gonna

00:00:06.744 --> 00:00:08.078
find happiness like it's Europe

00:00:08.078 --> 00:00:10.381
and they're never
gonna move out. (laughs)

00:00:10.381 --> 00:00:12.983
Happiness is a
byproduct of certain behaviors

00:00:12.983 --> 00:00:14.551
and can set yourself up to win

00:00:14.551 --> 00:00:16.520
and you can set
yourself up to be happy.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.289
The sad thing is happiness is a
learned skill and a lot of our

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:21.358
houses don't teach happiness.

00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:23.657
That was the situation
I was in and so I actually just

00:00:23.657 --> 00:00:25.095
started studying
people that were happy

00:00:25.095 --> 00:00:27.131
and I saw what
the algorithm was.

00:00:27.131 --> 00:00:30.734
What did they do that's similar
and for me I don't focus on

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.202
happiness as much as harmony.

00:00:32.202 --> 00:00:34.705
I don't really believe in the
word balance 'cause balance is a

00:00:34.705 --> 00:00:38.742
binary thing like oof,
it's a great very tedious.

00:00:39.962 --> 00:00:42.536
Harmony is saying my
life has many components.

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:45.916
I'm a woman,
I'm a mom,

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:48.355
I am sexual,
I am spiritual.

00:00:48.355 --> 00:00:52.559
I'm a businessperson, all of
those limbs have to have tone

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:53.827
and that brings about harmony.

00:00:53.827 --> 00:00:55.596
That brings about satisfaction.

00:00:55.596 --> 00:00:57.666
If only have one limb
that is very buff and

00:00:57.666 --> 00:00:59.139
the rest of us is atrophied,

00:00:59.139 --> 00:01:02.035
we have disharmony,
we have dissatisfaction but

00:01:02.035 --> 00:01:03.137
there's no human school and

00:01:03.137 --> 00:01:04.638
so that's what I'm
looking at starting.

00:01:04.638 --> 00:01:06.974
I want to be able to teach
people emotional and mindfulness

00:01:06.974 --> 00:01:09.743
skills so that they can
gain tone in every area.

00:01:09.743 --> 00:01:13.013
- From my standpoint, you know
since Jewel took it up here,

00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:15.799
I will take into one very narrow
place that I've been really

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:18.919
trying to spend a lot of time
on and that's perspective.

00:01:18.919 --> 00:01:22.956
It's so interesting to me why
I deem myself happy because

00:01:22.956 --> 00:01:25.092
I just am so grateful.
- Mhmmm.

00:01:25.092 --> 00:01:29.222
- Like the thing we got excited
about of you know the data

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:32.099
behind being a human
being is 400 trillion to 1.

00:01:32.099 --> 00:01:35.335
When you just start there and
you realize forget about the

00:01:35.335 --> 00:01:37.704
odds of like beating
homelessness and like other or

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.474
like being born in a communist
country like just actually

00:01:40.474 --> 00:01:42.546
becoming a human.

00:01:42.546 --> 00:01:43.610
I always make the joke that your

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:47.089
